Z||000018||AusFiero||08-11-2001||07:37 PM||||Well to answer a few questions. It is in Photoshop. Yes it is getting made. It will be made within the next 5 weeks if the orders keep coming in for the other products so I can afford to fund it. The pattern making and moulds don't come cheap, even doing them myself. But if you want the hood vents I noticed you asked for in anther thread Doni I could probably rush that bit along to be ready in about 2 weeks or less, something to do inbetween curing times on othr things.<P>Oh, and no I am not overdoing things. I work short hours and it has been a month now since surgery. Another month or 2 and I will be totally back to normal, well better than normal because I felt better days after surgery than I had felt in the 3 years previous.<p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Songman||08-11-2001||09:19 PM||||Aus, how much of the original fascia is used? Is the entire grill cut-out replaced or just the center V added? And what about molding in the vents at the top. Looks like you won't have much room to work it from the back...  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||AusFiero||08-11-2001||09:30 PM||||Most of the original fascia stays Songman. There will be enough room for all the new bits to bolt in and be stuck with an epoxy two part glue (or double sided tape, automotive grade) that can stick the 2 types of material together. The reperesentation does not show the flanges very well. Also you will have to remove your fascia to fit the parts. The lower grill sction is actually larger than an original Fiero one. I just got sick of drawing and didnt put the outer flange on it. Ther is other grill options that will be available also.<P>I could make complete fascias but that then leaves no option for mix and match pieces and would cost me a fortune to cover every possible combination of parts I designed.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000021||Fatal Error||08-11-2001||09:51 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Most of the original fascia stays Songman. There will be enough room for all the new bits to bolt in and be stuck with an epoxy two part glue (or double sided tape, automotive grade) that can stick the 2 types of material together. The representation does not show the flanges very well. Also you will have to remove your fascia to fit the parts. The lower grill section is actually larger than an original Fiero one. I just got sick of drawing and didn't put the outer flange on it. There is other grill options that will be available also.<P>I could make complete fascias but that then leaves no option for mix and match pieces and would cost me a fortune to cover every possible combination of parts I designed.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Great work Aus! I have a question. Would it be possible to create an optional fascia to go with your different trim/molding pieces? What I am getting at is I think if you took the design you have in your picture and made it onto a fascia that looked like the one from the 89-90 prototype, that would be unbelievably awesome. I'm not sure if I'm saying this right, so let me try it this way. Imagine the front of the 89-90 prototype, ok, now imagine it with the stage2 mods on it. ...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .. that would look very sharp. I like how the body lines come off of the front parking lights. Anyhow, just a thought. Please let me know if you think I'm dumb or just crazy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ... Take it easy!<P>-Fatal <P>P.S.<BR>what's with those lil' round holes at the bottom on each side of the venting? They kinda look cool, but was curious as for their purpose. Also have you tested any of this or other design for there aerodynamic properties? Thanks!<p>[This message has been edited by Fatal Error (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000022||AusFiero||08-11-2001||09:58 PM||||I have an 89 hybrid design that will take the stage 2 parts. Future project. The botton holes can be used for driving lights or for ducting air to the front brakes, or even to the radiator.||||reg||1
